{
  "_": "The raw-material price list, and the ONLY place material names live. Ships inside the app; a price change goes out as a release.",
  "_source": "Vansh's costing sheet, 2026-08-07 (WW-115), renamed and re-categorised to one scheme.",
  "_naming": "One shape for every row: `<Variant> <Item Type>`, Title Case, singular — 'Golden Star Foil', not 'Star Foil Golden' or 'STAR FOIL GOLDEN'. Word order does not affect matching, but a consistent list is one a person can scan. Sizes and counts that are part of the product's identity go after a comma ('Animal Set, 5 pcs').",
  "_aka": "Old names from the original sheet. They still MATCH — the partner's existing inventory pictures and every kit saved before the rename use them, and a cleanup that breaks yesterday's data is not a cleanup. Add to this list rather than renaming, whenever a name changes.",
  "_paise": "Cost of ONE unit in integer paise. `null` means the material is real but its price cell is BLANK in the sheet. The panel says 'no price set', which is a different problem from 'not on the list' and has a different fix. It is never treated as free.",
  "_categories": "Balloon (latex) · Foil Balloon · Banner · Curtain (was the opaque 'KT') · Themed Set (multi-piece character kits, which used to be split across 'Character' and 'Kit') · Decoration (standalone props, nets, lights, ribbon — was 'Extra'/'Net'/'LED') · Sash · Adhesive (was 'Tape') · Equipment · Packaging. The last two never appear on an inventory sheet; they are here so nothing is lost, not because a kit contains them.",
  "_sizes": "No size field yet — WW-116. Do not fill these in from the web; they come from the stock.",
